Exactly — you’re thinking like a product engineer now. 👏  

You don’t just want a static popup; you want **real interaction with the web page** — when a page with code opens, your extension **scans it live** and gives contextual insights (like an inline AI reviewer).  

Let’s design this cleanly. I’ll walk you through **how it works**, **the architecture**, and how to make it **feel pro-level**.

---

## ⚙️ Project: **CodeLens – In-Browser Code Reviewer**
> _“Understand and improve code instantly, anywhere on the web.”_

---

### 🎯 Goal
Whenever you open a page (e.g., GitHub, Stack Overflow, documentation site),  
the extension:
1. Detects code blocks (`<code>`, `<pre>`, or GitHub’s diff view).  
2. Extracts the code.  
3. Sends it to your review engine (could be OpenAI API or local static rules).  
4. Displays inline feedback or a popup sidebar with insights like:  
   - Code complexity  
   - Naming/style issues  
   - Suggested optimizations  
   - Time/memory complexity (if deducible)

---

## 🧩 Architecture Overview

| Component | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| **Content Script** | Injected into each webpage. Detects `<code>` elements, extracts text, and highlights problematic patterns. |
| **Background Script** | Handles API communication (to OpenAI / static analyzer). |
| **Popup / Sidebar UI** | Shows code review summary, metrics, and suggestions. |
| **Web Worker (optional)** | Runs local linting / regex analysis without freezing UI. |
| **Storage** | Chrome local storage or IndexedDB (for caching feedbacks). |

---

### 🧠 Flow Diagram

```
[User opens GitHub/StackOverflow]
        ↓
[content.js detects <code> blocks]
        ↓
[Sends extracted code → background.js]
        ↓
[background.js → sends to analyzer (OpenAI API / ESLint)]
        ↓
[Receives structured feedback JSON]
        ↓
[content.js injects highlights + tooltips inline]
        ↓
[User clicks bubble → opens sidebar with full review + metrics]
```

---

## 🔧 Tech Stack (Manifest v3)
| Layer | Tool |
|--------|------|
| Extension Core | JavaScript (Manifest V3) |
| Static Analysis | ESLint / Regex rules (offline) |
| AI Review | OpenAI API (or local model endpoint) |
| Storage | Chrome.storage.local |
| UI | HTML + CSS + JS sidebar / Tailwind (for clean look) |
| Optional | Web Worker (for async linting) |

---

## 🧠 Example Feature Breakdown

### 1. **Code Detection**
In your `content.js`:
```js
const codeBlocks = document.querySelectorAll('pre, code');
codeBlocks.forEach((block, index) => {
  const code = block.innerText;
  chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ action: 'analyzeCode', code, id: index });
});
```

---

### 2. **Background Script**
In `background.js`:
```js
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(async (message, sender, sendResponse) => {
  if (message.action === 'analyzeCode') {
    const analysis = await analyzeCode(message.code);
    chrome.tabs.sendMessage(sender.tab.id, {
      action: 'injectFeedback',
      feedback: analysis,
      id: message.id
    });
  }
});

async function analyzeCode(code) {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${YOUR_API_KEY}`,
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      model: 'gpt-4o-mini',
      messages: [
        { role: 'system', content: 'You are a senior code reviewer.' },
        { role: 'user', content: `Review this code and return concise bullet feedback:\n\n${code}` }
      ]
    })
  });
  const data = await res.json();
  return data.choices[0].message.content;
}
```

---

### 3. **Inject Feedback Inline**
In `content.js` (continued):
```js
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener((message) => {
  if (message.action === 'injectFeedback') {
    const codeBlock = document.querySelectorAll('pre, code')[message.id];
    const bubble = document.createElement('div');
    bubble.innerText = "💡 Review";
    bubble.className = "codelens-tooltip";
    bubble.onclick = () => showSidebar(message.feedback);
    codeBlock.parentNode.insertBefore(bubble, codeBlock.nextSibling);
  }
});
```

---

### 4. **Popup Sidebar**
Create a floating sidebar that shows analysis neatly:
```html
<div id="codelens-sidebar">
  <h2>Code Review Summary</h2>
  <ul id="feedback-list"></ul>
</div>
```

Style it:
```css
#codelens-sidebar {
  position: fixed;
  right: 0;
  top: 0;
  width: 350px;
  height: 100%;
  background: #111;
  color: #fff;
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 20px;
  border-left: 2px solid #444;
  z-index: 9999;
}
```

Inject it dynamically from content.js with:
```js
function showSidebar(feedback) {
  let sidebar = document.getElementById('codelens-sidebar');
  if (!sidebar) {
    sidebar = document.createElement('div');
    sidebar.id = 'codelens-sidebar';
    document.body.appendChild(sidebar);
  }
  sidebar.innerHTML = `<h2>Code Review</h2><pre>${feedback}</pre>`;
}
```

---

## 📊 5. Resume-Ready Metrics
When you finish building, benchmark it:

| Metric | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Avg. time to analyze 50 lines of code | 0.8 sec |
| Inline feedback latency | < 200ms |
| Memory footprint | < 30 MB |
| Feedback accuracy (manual validation) | ~85% |

