Got it — you want **CodeLens** to work *automatically* across **any webpage** that contains code snippets — not just GitHub or Stack Overflow.  

So when a person opens a page, **your extension quietly scans** for any `<code>` or `<pre>` blocks, **analyzes them**, and **displays helpful insights inline or in a floating panel** — no manual click needed.  

This version is a **“passive intelligence layer”** on top of the web. Let’s break down exactly how you’d build it.  

---

## 🧠 Concept: CodeLens (Auto-Active Code Insight Layer)

**Goal:**  
Whenever any webpage with code is loaded, CodeLens automatically:
1. Detects code snippets (HTML `<code>`, `<pre>`, fenced Markdown, etc.)  
2. Determines the programming language (simple heuristic).  
3. Sends snippets for static or AI analysis.  
4. Inserts an inline “💡 Insights” bubble near each block.  
5. When hovered or clicked, displays a pop-up with concise review points.

---

## ⚙️ High-Level Architecture

| Layer | Function |
|--------|-----------|
| **Manifest V3** | Declares permissions (activeTab, scripting, storage) |
| **Content Script** | Scans every loaded webpage for `<code>`/`<pre>` elements |
| **Background Service Worker** | Handles heavy logic + API calls (e.g., OpenAI, ESLint) |
| **UI Layer** | Tooltip / sidebar injected dynamically |
| **Local Storage** | Caches analysis results per URL (to avoid re-analyzing) |

---

## 🧩 Core Flow

```
[User loads any webpage]
   ↓
[content.js scans DOM for code]
   ↓
[Each snippet → background.js for analysis]
   ↓
[background.js → OpenAI API / ESLint]
   ↓
[Returns JSON feedback]
   ↓
[content.js injects tooltips & side panel with review]
```

---

## 🔧 Implementation Sketch

### 1️⃣ manifest.json

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "CodeLens",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Auto code reviewer for any webpage",
  "permissions": ["activeTab", "scripting", "storage"],
  "background": { "service_worker": "background.js" },
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content.js"],
      "run_at": "document_end"
    }
  ],
  "action": {
    "default_icon": "icon.png",
    "default_popup": "popup.html"
  }
}
```

---

### 2️⃣ content.js

```js
// Detect <code> or <pre> blocks
const codeBlocks = document.querySelectorAll('pre, code');
if (codeBlocks.length > 0) {
  codeBlocks.forEach((block, i) => {
    const code = block.innerText.trim();
    if (code.split('\n').length > 2) { // Ignore short snippets
      chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ action: "analyze", id: i, code });
    }
  });
}

// Listen for injected feedback
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener((msg) => {
  if (msg.action === "injectFeedback") {
    const target = document.querySelectorAll('pre, code')[msg.id];
    if (!target) return;
    const tag = document.createElement('div');
    tag.innerText = "💡 View Insight";
    tag.className = "codelens-tag";
    tag.onclick = () => showInsights(msg.feedback);
    target.parentNode.insertBefore(tag, target);
  }
});

function showInsights(feedback) {
  let panel = document.getElementById('codelens-panel');
  if (!panel) {
    panel = document.createElement('div');
    panel.id = 'codelens-panel';
    panel.style.cssText = `
      position:fixed; right:0; top:0; width:400px; height:100%;
      background:#111; color:#fff; padding:16px; overflow:auto;
      z-index:999999; border-left:2px solid #444; font-family:monospace;
    `;
    document.body.appendChild(panel);
  }
  panel.innerHTML = `<h3>Code Review</h3><pre>${feedback}</pre>`;
}
```

---

### 3️⃣ background.js

```js
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(async (msg, sender) => {
  if (msg.action === "analyze") {
    const result = await analyzeCode(msg.code);
    chrome.tabs.sendMessage(sender.tab.id, {
      action: "injectFeedback",
      id: msg.id,
      feedback: result
    });
  }
});

async function analyzeCode(code) {
  try {
    const res = await fetch("https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
        "Authorization": `Bearer ${YOUR_API_KEY}`
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        model: "gpt-4o-mini",
        messages: [
          { role: "system", content: "You are a senior code reviewer. Be concise." },
          { role: "user", content: `Review and summarize issues:\n${code}` }
        ]
      })
    });
    const data = await res.json();
    return data.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || "No feedback";
  } catch (e) {
    return `Error analyzing: ${e.message}`;
  }
}
```

