### 🔍 OPTIONAL ENHANCEMENTS

**1. Debounce Scanning:**  
If the page dynamically loads code (e.g., GitHub, Reddit), you can re-scan every few seconds:
```js
setInterval(scanForNewCode, 3000);
```

**2. Lazy Feedback Injection:**  
Instead of analyzing all at once, analyze only when user scrolls into view (saves API usage).

**3. Local Cache:**  
Store results in `chrome.storage.local`:
```js
chrome.storage.local.set({ [url]: feedback });
```

So you don’t analyze the same code twice.

