## 🧩 1️⃣ Injecting the “💡 Insights” Badge

In your `content.js`, we already added this:

```js
function injectFeedback(id, feedback) {
  const block = document.querySelector(`[data-codelens-id="${id}"]`);
  if (!block) return;

  const tag = document.createElement("div");
  tag.innerText = "💡 Insights";
  tag.className = "codelens-badge";

  tag.onclick = () => showSidebar(feedback);

  block.parentNode.insertBefore(tag, block.nextSibling);
}
```

This adds a tiny badge directly after every code block.  
Each badge is lightweight — about ~10 lines of HTML per block.  

✅ **Why not buttons or popups?**
- Popups often get blocked by Chrome or the site’s JS.
- Inline badges are more natural and easy to position.

