## 🧩 2️⃣ The Sidebar UI (the Main Review Window)

We’ll create a **floating sidebar** that slides in from the right side of the screen — similar to a developer console.

```js
function showSidebar(feedback) {
  let panel = document.getElementById("codelens-panel");
  if (!panel) {
    panel = document.createElement("div");
    panel.id = "codelens-panel";
    panel.innerHTML = `
      <div id="codelens-header">
        <span>🧠 CodeLens Review</span>
        <button id="close-panel">×</button>
      </div>
      <pre id="codelens-feedback"></pre>
    `;
    document.body.appendChild(panel);

    // close button event
    document.getElementById("close-panel").onclick = () => {
      panel.remove();
    };
  }

  document.getElementById("codelens-feedback").innerText = feedback;
}
```

### 🧠 How It Works
- Checks if the sidebar already exists (so you don’t duplicate it).
- If not, it builds one dynamically and attaches it to `<body>`.  
- Adds a close (×) button for clean UX.
- Displays formatted feedback as preformatted text.

