## 🧩 1️⃣ Caching with `chrome.storage.local`

Each time a code snippet is analyzed, store its feedback locally so the same code never hits the API again.

```js
async function getCachedFeedback(codeHash) {
  return new Promise(resolve => {
    chrome.storage.local.get(codeHash, data => resolve(data[codeHash]));
  });
}

async function setCachedFeedback(codeHash, feedback) {
  chrome.storage.local.set({ [codeHash]: feedback });
}
```

In `background.js`:

```js
async function analyzeCode(code) {
  const hash = await digestMessage(code);  // tiny hash helper below
  const cached = await getCachedFeedback(hash);
  if (cached) return cached; // ✅ instant return

  const feedback = await callHuggingFace(code);
  await setCachedFeedback(hash, feedback);
  return feedback;
}

async function digestMessage(message) {
  const msgUint8 = new TextEncoder().encode(message);
  const hashBuffer = await crypto.subtle.digest("SHA-256", msgUint8);
  const hashArray = Array.from(new Uint8Array(hashBuffer));
  return hashArray.map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
}
```

✅ **Why:**  
- Avoids duplicate API calls → faster and cheaper.  
- Makes your extension feel “instant” on repeated visits.  

---

## 🧩 2️⃣ Async Execution & Web Workers

**Problem:** Long analysis (API or lint) can freeze Chrome tabs.  
**Fix:** Use Web Workers or async Promises.

Because `background.js` is already a **service worker**, it runs asynchronously by design.  
Still, inside content scripts, avoid synchronous loops:

```js
async function scanPage() {
  const blocks = document.querySelectorAll("pre, code");
  for (const block of blocks) {
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100)); // small delay
    // send messages gradually, not all at once
  }
}
```

✅ **Why:** Prevents CPU spikes on big pages (like long StackOverflow threads).

---

## 🧩 3️⃣ Rate Limiting API Calls

Even free APIs like Hugging Face have limits (~30–50 req/hr).  
We’ll add a simple throttle:

```js
let lastCall = 0;
const API_INTERVAL = 5000; // 1 call / 5s

async function safeApiCall(fn) {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - lastCall < API_INTERVAL) {
    console.log("⏳ Waiting to avoid rate limit...");
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, API_INTERVAL - (now - lastCall)));
  }
  lastCall = Date.now();
  return fn();
}
```

Usage:
```js
const feedback = await safeApiCall(() => callHuggingFace(code));
```

✅ **Why:** Prevents your extension from getting temporarily blocked.

